    "updated_at": "2020-09-02T13:05:16Z",
    "body": "Could an alternative be to tackle this through https://heycam.github.io/webidl/#es-type-mapping? That we assert that the JS value is not a Window object and when given a JS WindowProxy object, we return the IDL Window object for the JS WindowProxy's [[Window]] object? And that an IDL Window object is mapped back to a JS WindowProxy object (it seems this would have to go through the browsing context which isn't ideal).",
